---
title: "get_last_256_block_hashes (Osaka Fork - Ethereum Execution Specification)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_slice: recent_blocks = chain.blocks[-255:]
    q_slice --> q_check_empty: len(recent_blocks) == 0
    q_check_empty --> q_return_empty: true
    q_return_empty --> [*]: return []
    q_check_empty --> q_init_list: false
    q_init_list --> q_iter: recent_block_hashes = []
    q_iter --> q_append: for block in recent_blocks
    q_append --> q_iter: append(block.header.parent_hash)
    q_iter --> q_hash_recent: loop done
    q_hash_recent --> q_append_final: most_recent_block_hash = keccak256(rlp.encode(recent_blocks[-1].header))
    q_append_final --> q_return: append(most_recent_block_hash)
    q_return --> [*]: return recent_block_hashes
    note right of q_return
        INV-001: Returns at most 256 hashes
        INV-002: Hashes are in order of increasing block number
        INV-003: Only the most recent block hash is computed via keccak256; others use parent_hash from successors
    end note
